<objective>
Build the TEE-based pin migration backend infrastructure. When a user switches providers, their existing encrypted pins need to be moved from source to destination. The TEE worker handles the actual data transfer (opaque encrypted blobs) while the API orchestrates jobs via BullMQ.

Purpose: Per user decision, switching providers triggers background migration via TEE. The TEE worker decrypts provider credentials in-enclave, fetches encrypted blobs from the source, pins to the destination, and verifies CID integrity. This preserves zero-knowledge -- the TEE never sees plaintext content, only encrypted ciphertext.

Output: Migration entity, service, controller, BullMQ processor in API. Migration endpoint and worker in TEE.
</objective>

